1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,062
The History of Money.

2
00:00:02,012 --> 00:00:06,812
Before coinage, barter required mutual desire for each other's goods.

3
00:00:06,812 --> 00:00:15,062
The first standardized currency appeared around 5,000 years ago in Mesopotamia, where silver bars served as medium of exchange.

4
00:00:15,062 --> 00:00:18,612
China introduced paper money in the 7th century.

5
00:00:18,612 --> 00:00:25,675
The Latin word sal (salt) gave rise to salary, as Roman soldiers were occasionally paid in salt.

6
00:00:25,675 --> 00:00:33,537
Gold-backed currencies dominated international trade from the 19th century until the 1971 collapse of the Bretton Woods system.

7
00:00:33,537 --> 00:00:42,425
Today, over 90 percent of money exists only as electronic records; physical cash represents a small fraction of global monetary supply.

8
00:00:42,425 --> 00:00:49,437
Cryptocurrencies represent a further evolution: decentralized digital money verified by blockchain technology.

